No score assigned.

Accepted new evidence

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Biden: Putin Invasion Would be 'War of Choice'","publisher":"Voice of America (VOA News)","publication_date":"2022-02-15","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/biden-putin-invasion-would-be-war-of-choice-/6443727.html","claim":"Biden said a Russian invasion of Ukraine would be a 'war of choice' that would inflict needless death and destruction.","locator":"line 86","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous reporting of Biden's own warning.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct February 2022 pre-invasion warning.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution to Biden's own public statement.","contrary_evidence":["This is warning rhetoric rather than a completed peace or restraint outcome."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Biden Announces $800 Million in New Ukraine Assistance, Calls Putin 'a War Criminal'","publisher":"Voice of America (VOA News)","publication_date":"2022-03-16","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/biden-announces-new-assistance-after-zelenskyy-asks-for-more-us-help/6488192.html","claim":"Biden approved an $800 million Ukraine assistance package and the report says the package fell short of Zelenskyy's requested no-fly zone.","locator":"lines 94-106","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous reporting of Biden's announced action and its restraint limit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct March 2022 wartime policy choice.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution to Biden's decision, with some factual dependence on reporter framing of the no-fly-zone comparison.","contrary_evidence":["The package still escalated military support to Ukraine."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.5","2B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Inside President Biden's often impulsive approach to the war in Ukraine","publisher":"The Washington Post","publication_date":"2022-04-07","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/04/07/biden-war-ukraine/","claim":"Biden said he would not send U.S. combat troops or support a no-fly zone, and he decided not to help transfer Polish MiG-29s because it could be seen as direct U.S. involvement.","locator":"lines 135-136","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting based on interviews with senior officials and direct decision details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct April 2022 restraint decision during the Ukraine war.","ruler_attribution":"Strong attribution to Biden, though the article is a reconstruction from officials rather than a presidential transcript.","contrary_evidence":["The same period also included expanding sanctions and weapons transfers."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.5","2B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine, Russia sign deal to reopen grain export ports as war rages on","publisher":"Euronews","publication_date":"2022-07-22","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/07/22/uk-ukraine-crisis","claim":"Russia and Ukraine signed a UN- and Turkey-brokered grain export deal that opened three Ukrainian ports and created a coordination centre to monitor implementation.","locator":"lines 659-661","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-reported summary carried by Euronews with concrete deal terms and implementation mechanism.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct July 2022 conflict-management and food-security outcome.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the deal was part of the wider U.S.-backed effort to manage the war without direct U.S.-Russia combat.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not itself describe a direct Biden order or personal negotiation role."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Wheat prices rise as missile strike threatens Ukraine export pact","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-07-25","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/commodities-news/wheat-prices-rise-as-missile-strike-threatens-ukraine-export-pact-2852939","claim":"A Russian missile strike on Odesa immediately raised doubts about implementing the grain-export corridor, even though the deal reopened three Black Sea ports for 120 days and targeted 5 million tonnes per month.","locator":"lines 406-418","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting with direct operational detail on a fragile peace mechanism.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct July 2022 implementation stress test of the grain deal.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but useful for Biden's peace-management record because it shows the fragility of the corridor his administration publicly backed.","contrary_evidence":["The piece is about implementation risk, not Biden's own conduct."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Seafarer shortage stands in way of Ukraine grain corridor","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-07-27","url":"https://uk.investing.com/news/commodities-news/seafarer-shortage-stands-in-way-of-ukraine-grain-corridor-2699280","claim":"Reuters reported that about 80 ships remained blocked in Ukraine and that crew security and mine-clearing were major obstacles to turning the grain corridor into a safe passage route.","locator":"lines 424-437","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting with concrete operational constraints and safety issues.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct July 2022 corridor-implementation context.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context: it shows the practical limits on the peace corridor Biden backed, not his direct command.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not attribute the bottlenecks to Biden."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bulk carrier sets off from Ukraine with grain for WFP in first since start of war","publisher":"World Food Programme","publication_date":"2022-08-16","url":"https://www.wfp.org/stories/bulk-carrier-sets-ukraine-grain-wfp-first-start-war","claim":"The Brave Commander carried 23,000 metric tons of Ukrainian wheat to the Horn of Africa, one of the first wartime grain shipments under the Black Sea Initiative, to help feed a drought-hit and food-insecure region.","locator":"lines 259-266, 274-275","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary humanitarian agency reporting on a concrete shipment and its intended beneficiaries.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct August 2022 downstream result of the Black Sea corridor.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: this is an observable humanitarian effect of the peace corridor supported by Biden's administration.","contrary_evidence":["This measures one shipment, not the whole war or all food-security effects."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine: Amid mounting human cost, parties must uphold international humanitarian law","publisher":"International Committee of the Red Cross","publication_date":"2022-03-04","url":"https://www.icrc.org/en/document/ukraine-amid-mounting-human-cost-parties-must-uphold-international-humanitarian-law-0","claim":"The ICRC urged all parties to spare the civilian population from military operations and immediately allow safe passage for people fleeing the fighting.","locator":"lines 191-192","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Authoritative humanitarian-law statement from the ICRC during the opening phase of the war.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct March 2022 conflict-law context.","ruler_attribution":"Context only: it does not attribute the legal obligation to Biden, but it defines the conduct environment for U.S. choices.","contrary_evidence":["General IHL guidance, not a Biden-specific finding."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia-Ukraine: Civilian lives and infrastructure must be protected","publisher":"International Committee of the Red Cross","publication_date":"2022-10-10","url":"https://www.icrc.org/en/document/ukrainerussia-civilian-lives-and-infrastructure-must-be-protected","claim":"The ICRC said explosive weapons in populated areas put civilians in peril and disrupt essential services such as water, electricity, sanitation, and health care, with the most severe impact on children, the elderly, and disabled people.","locator":"lines 179-188","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Authoritative 2022 ICRC field statement on civilian harm and infrastructure damage.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct October 2022 conflict context.","ruler_attribution":"Context only: it is not a Biden action, but it sharpens the civilian-protection stakes of U.S. policy choices.","contrary_evidence":["General humanitarian context rather than direct ruler conduct."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Biden Warns Putin on Use of WMDs: 'Don't, Don't, Don't'","publisher":"Voice of America (VOA News)","publication_date":"2022-09-17","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/biden-warns-putin-on-use-of-weapons-of-mass-destruction/6751789.html","claim":"Biden warned Putin not to use weapons of mass destruction in Ukraine, saying it would change the face of war and that NATO would respond in kind to any WMD use.","locator":"lines 92-101","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous report of Biden's televised warning and its stated escalation logic.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct September 2022 coercive-security choice during the Ukraine war.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution to Biden's own warning.","contrary_evidence":["This is deterrent rhetoric rather than a peace settlement or ceasefire."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"US Warns Russia of 'Catastrophic Consequences' If It Launches Nuclear Attack in Ukraine","publisher":"Voice of America (VOA News)","publication_date":"2022-09-25","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/us-warns-russia-of-catastrophic-consequences-if-it-launches-nuclear-attack-in-ukraine-/6762441.html","claim":"The U.S. privately warned Russia of catastrophic consequences if it launched a nuclear attack in Ukraine and deliberately kept the response vague rather than engaging in rhetorical tit-for-tat.","locator":"lines 94-99","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of U.S. private messaging and deterrence posture from Biden's national-security adviser.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct September 2022 crisis-management posture.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution to Biden's administration through Sullivan's description of private U.S. messaging.","contrary_evidence":["The report still concerns deterrence, not a negotiated peace settlement."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.9","2B.10"]}

Search ledger
- Candidates found: about 40
- Documents opened: 19 promising docs
- Duplicates removed: 10
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items: 7
- Inaccessible items: 5
- Accepted distinct URLs: 11

Gaps
- Direct private deconfliction and ceasefire-channel management: partly resolved.
- Whether the 2022 U.S. approach shortened, prolonged, or merely stabilized the war: not recoverable in this wave.
- Direct attribution of proxy-control and civilian-harm restraint to Biden beyond support, sanctions, weapons, and deterrence: partly resolved.
- Durability of the Black Sea corridor and other peace mechanisms into 2023: partly resolved, but still not a complete end-state answer.
- Blockers: several `state.gov` archive pages returned technical difficulties or `forbidden`, some Reuters/Investing URLs had cache misses, and a few AP/PBS pages were 403 or out of period, so I excluded them.
